※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4918
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4918 LANG_CLAUSE_CANNOT_HOLD

※ A condition over the types is settled at the call, so a type the function was
※ not meant for is refused there rather than wherever its body first goes wrong.

type A = n : u8
type B = n : u8

fn make(kind: ⌜T'⌝, v: u8) → T'
        pre(⌜T'⌝ = ⌜A⌝ ∨ ⌜T'⌝ = ⌜B⌝):
    comptime if ⌜T'⌝ = ⌜A⌝:
        A(.n ← v)
    else:
        B(.n ← v)

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let x: u8 = make(⌜u8⌝, 3u8)
    if x = 3u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
